  "subtitle": "A wire-impregnated chart table that guides your hand by four LEDs to the vessel's live position",
  "why_scout_cares": "The museum's only embodied hand-tracking navigation device: four illuminated arrows on a 'mouse' race toward the live GPS position until they all extinguish and you mark the fix with a pencil through a hole. The display is a 35-inch paper chart; your whole arm is the pointing mechanism. Nothing else in the collection guides a human hand by feedback to a moving target while reading position from the geometry of where you are.",
